{
  "name": "city-budget-brief-multiple-footnotes-body-paragraphs-v2",
  "description": "A short policy brief with several body paragraphs that each contain multiple footnote references, testing how repeated inline notes are preserved across paragraphs.",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Downtown Mobility Budget Brief"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "The draft budget shifts operating funds from peak-hour parking enforcement"
        },
        {
          "text": "1",
          "sup": true,
          "footnote": "Parking enforcement redeployment is described in the March staffing memo approved by the transportation committee."
        },
        {
          "text": " to evening bus frequency pilots in the central corridor"
        },
        {
          "text": "2",
          "sup": true,
          "footnote": "The pilot covers Route 6 and Route 14 between 6 p.m. and 10 p.m. on weekdays."
        },
        {
          "text": ", with the stated goal of reducing wait times before winter service changes take effect."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Analysts note that the projected ridership gain depends on temporary signal-priority equipment"
        },
        {
          "text": "3",
          "sup": true,
          "footnote": "Temporary signal-priority units are leased for nine months and require separate maintenance funding."
        },
        {
          "text": " and on extending the regional fare cap to municipal passes"
        },
        {
          "text": "4",
          "sup": true,
          "footnote": "The fare-cap extension is contingent on a data-sharing agreement with the regional transit authority."
        },
        {
          "text": ", neither of which is fully funded in the current ordinance."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "runs": [
        {
          "text": "Council staff also warned that storefront loading zones may be reduced on two blocks near the market"
        },
        {
          "text": "5",
          "sup": true,
          "footnote": "The affected blocks are on Alder Street between 3rd and 5th Avenue."
        },
        {
          "text": ", a tradeoff merchants accepted only after the city promised a six-month review"
        },
        {
          "text": "6",
          "sup": true,
          "footnote": "The review period begins after installation and includes monthly delivery-time observations."
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
